#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186286109 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "b4df33ff-e04e-55ec-b273-9eceff7db53b" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Rotation Matrices"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "06c787d6-689a-5822-8a86-85ec0b629d8d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14003089/assets/90dcf60e19c9031927df68a1d0be6b85c47910e6ec92e9052c292f667971d7f1.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286111} {:answer/id #uuid "e1439b53-eca2-5bbf-b769-42c54ff2d285" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14003089/assets/805c480c5341b6fbf3e8d5720187fead535db2a651939572a3a9faf453726087.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286112} {:answer/id #uuid "0f707bbe-3259-5697-89af-24c9ef4e1be0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14003089/assets/ba328088ca187ea28b241a302a486da1145a51c7e134d8d4f529f5f4a916ddc1.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286113} {:answer/id #uuid "d6c1d14d-be0f-5784-904b-646847e99b1d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14003089/assets/9dc6d9d844c382cc5a8499929dfe7d3a9ab8bf59fc5b73b2cd4dab44c51e135f.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286114} {:answer/id #uuid "69d2f542-abdb-5ecf-8d1d-a682af96b739" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14003089/assets/c612d528e8fb432e4f63fdaae2649a4a41b0f3bed7751df5b5cc22074b57bb53.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286115}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d6c1d14d-be0f-5784-904b-646847e99b1d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14003089/assets/9dc6d9d844c382cc5a8499929dfe7d3a9ab8bf59fc5b73b2cd4dab44c51e135f.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286114} :answer-field/id #uuid "566ece9b-df45-52fe-953c-549c09e7bf67" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286110}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "cec76be9-565e-5e8f-a9d4-8ee2ab561594" :question/math-academy-id "q-160624" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14003089/assets/c32886c161e347daa9bf6fa7215f8a09abc4334632c33020c31ade6dfc4e7315.png)\n\nConsider the vector $v$ shown above. Find the vector $Av$ given that \n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{aligned}].\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Consider the standard basis ${i,j}$ of the Euclidean plane ${R}^{2}$ and the unit square spanned by the vectors. Computing the images of ${i,j}$ under $A$, we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{i}^{′} & =A(i)=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]=-i \\\\ {j}^{′} & =A(j)=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]=-j\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAs a result, we obtain the following diagram:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14003089/assets/9fae3ec0ada3008937d88e4e76374a56da4369b1821cfee072c90d88b562df46.png)\n\nSo, the matrix represents a rotation of $\\pi $ radians (counterclockwise or clockwise) about the origin.\n\nTherefore, in order to find $Av$, we need to rotate $v$ (counterclockwise or clockwise) by an angle of $\\pi $ radians, as shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14003089/assets/ed1a5e8a05ee0d9994d8ba90c02463fbf96525b1cd851bec685a005a34834f81.png)"}]}
